# The premise of `abstract ComputePAC` in every other PAC job, that the
# model's PAC algorithm is a function of its arguments (four; in the
# Armv9.4-A model five, the last `isgeneric`, false for `pacda`),
# spot-checked (verus/isla/seams.md): `pacda x0, x1` with
# ComputePAC unfolded, on concrete operands, key and PC (run-aarch64.sh
# section 6, eight inputs in the Armv8.5-A model and in the Armv9.4-A one
# with QARMA5 and with QARMA3), so the only symbols left in the trace are
# the model's undefined values and the initial contents of RC, ComputePAC's
# round-constant array. Copies `a` and `b` run the same trace, each with
# its own such symbols, and get the same result, which differs from the
# pointer (the PAC is applied). run.sh prepends the copy and insn lines
# (and `pc-step` for Armv9.4-A) and substitutes @P@ (the pointer).
writes R0 RC
no-mem-write
mem-reads 0
flags-preserved
assert (= a.final.R0 b.final.R0)
assert (not (= a.final.R0 @P@))
